body:
Removes the differential pair phase skew overlay (`showDifferentialPairPhaseSkew`, `phaseSkewColors`) along with its dependency on `circuit-json-to-differential-pair-phase-skew`.

The plan has changed. Core will compute phase skew and store it in Circuit JSON as `pcb_differential_pair_phase_skew` (circuit-json #1051, merged), so the renderer shouldn't compute it anymore. Drawing the stored element will be a separate PR once core writes it.

This PR removes:
- the overlay's svg-object function, its options, and its layer sort entry;
- the README lines for the two options;
- the `noExternal` bundle entry in `tsup.config.ts`;
- the library line in `package.json`;
- the phase skew tests, fixtures and snapshots;
- the `tscircuit-phase-skew-fixtures` dev dependency (`npm:tscircuit@0.0.3285`), which only those tests used.

`create-pcb-trace-stroke.ts`, which was split out in the same original PR, stays, because ordinary trace drawing uses it.

Behaviour change: `showDifferentialPairPhaseSkew` and `phaseSkewColors` are no longer accepted. Nothing outside these tests passed them.

Checked locally: `bunx tsc --noEmit` (with and without the alias), `bun run build`, `bun run format:check`, `bun test tests/pcb` (281 pass). The one failure is `pcb-return-current.test.ts`, which times out on main too.

